  'content/writings/indiemark-checklist.mdx':
    '---\ndescription: IndieMark gives me a checklist for testing independent publishing on willie.page.\npublished: 2026-09-23T18:51-0700\nlastUpdated: 2026-09-23T18:51-0700\ntags: [note, indieweb]\ndraft: true\npostType: note\ninReplyTo: https://indieweb.org/IndieMark\n---\n\nIndieMark gives me a checklist for testing independent publishing on\nwillie.page. An isolated copy of the site now publishes notes through Micropub,\nsends and receives Webmentions, and delivers feed updates through WebSub. I am\nkeeping the public level claim open until this domain has original posts,\nactual syndication copies, and a reply that another site displays.\n',
  'content/writings/project-superbloom.mdx':
    "---\ntitle: 'Project Superbloom'\ndescription: 'Introducing my ambitious plan to ship four products in one month.'\npublished: 2026-01-04T23:44-0800\nlastUpdated: 2026-01-04T23:44-0800\ntags: ['personal']\ndraft: true\nfeaturedImage: ''\nfeaturedImageAlt: ''\nseries:\n  slug: superbloom\n  part: 1\n---\n\n> Superbloom\n>\n> a rare desert botanical phenomenon in California and Arizona in which an\n> unusually high proportion of wildflowers whose seeds have lain dormant in\n> desert soil germinate and blossom at roughly the same time.\n\nI live in the Las Vegas metro area. Technically North Las Vegas, but such\na distinction is as generally useful as acknowlding that\n\nThis is the story all about how my life got flipped, turned upside down.\n\n# The Guy Who Peaked in College\n\nI attended The Uniersity of Texas at Dallas and majored in computer science.\n\n# What's in a Superbloom\n\nThe premise of Project Superbloom is simple: I will grow my collection of work\ninto a lush field of useful products and\n\nFrankly, I miss the days\n\n# A Diary\n\nI recognize that I gain a lot of value from creating\n\nThe Willie Diaries will be my way of connecting with\n\nAnd perhaps other strangers will find what I leave on the internet and be able\nto relate to me in ways I cannot anticipate.\n\n# Several Silly SaaS Apps\n\nI am going to do what was likely impossible this time last year: I am going to\nlaunch four different software products in a single month. Not because\n\n## Project Athena\n\n## Storyloom\n\nWhile there are other tools to help people storyboard,\n\n## Project Lovelace\n\n# Goals\n\nProject Superbloom answers one question: can I start doing big things again?\n\nThe labels for these goals are a little facetious, but they do embody my\nunderlying intents behind this initiative.\n\n## Do more things\n\nI've gotten comfortable\n\n## Do more important things\n\n## Do things more quickly\n\n<SpotifyEmbed url=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/2HvtedoEeymVWrBPyAMNwZ?si=a2f970f80ce24103\" />\n",
  'content/writings/testing-independent-publishing.mdx':
    '---\ntitle: Testing independent publishing on willie.page\ndescription: How I checked Micropub, Webmention, feeds, and WebSub before bringing them to my site.\npublished: 2026-09-23T18:51-0700\nlastUpdated: 2026-09-23T18:51-0700\ntags: [indieweb, website]\ndraft: true\npostType: article\n---\n\nI want my posts to live at URLs I control. I have added note publishing through\nMicropub, an author card and entry markup that other sites can parse, and RSS,\nAtom, and JSON feeds. The site also accepts Webmentions for moderation and sends\nthem when a post links to another site.\n\nI tested the writing flow on an isolated deployment with its own database,\nmedia store, and publishing branch. A Micropub request created a Git commit.\nThat commit deployed without a manual rebuild, and the new permalink appeared\nin the feeds. A subscriber at WebSub Rocks received the RSS update after the\ndeployment. I also checked that removing a link sends a fresh Webmention to\nthe former target and that removing a link from a mention source removes the\napproved interaction from the post.\n\nThose tests show that the pieces can work together. I still need to publish\noriginal posts on willie.page and link any copies on other services back to\ntheir originals before I claim an IndieMark level for the public site.\n',
